{"subjectId":"javascript","id":"json","title":"JSON","group":"Arrays & Objects","order":28,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">JSON is a text format for data, borrowed from JavaScript literal syntax. <code>JSON.stringify</code> serialises, <code>JSON.parse</code> deserialises — each with a hook for customisation.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-file-code\"></i>JSON vs JavaScript objects</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>JSON</th><th>JavaScript object literal</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Keys <strong>must</strong> be double-quoted strings</td><td>Keys can be bare identifiers</td></tr><tr><td>Strings in double quotes only</td><td><code>'single'</code>, <code>\"double\"</code> and backtick templates</td></tr><tr><td>Values: string, number, boolean, <code>null</code>, object, array</td><td>Also functions, <code>undefined</code>, symbols, BigInt, Date, Map…</td></tr><tr><td>No trailing commas, no comments</td><td>Trailing commas allowed</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-arrow-right\"></i>stringify</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const data = {\n  name: \"Asha\",\n  tags: [\"js\", \"node\"],\n  born: new Date(Date.UTC(1995, 11, 4)),\n  skip: undefined,\n  fn() {},\n  sym: Symbol(\"s\"),\n  nan: NaN,\n  inf: Infinity,\n};\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(data));\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify([undefined, () =&gt; {}, NaN]));\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify({ a: 1, b: [1, 2] }, null, 2));</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>{\"name\":\"Asha\",\"tags\":[\"js\",\"node\"],\"born\":\"1995-12-04T00:00:00.000Z\",\"nan\":null,\"inf\":null}\n[null,null,null]\n{\n  \"a\": 1,\n  \"b\": [\n    1,\n    2\n  ]\n}</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--warn\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Watch out</div><p>Silently lost: <code>undefined</code>, functions and symbols (dropped in objects, <code>null</code> in arrays); <code>NaN</code>/<code>Infinity</code> become <code>null</code>; <code>Date</code> becomes a string; <code>Map</code>/<code>Set</code> become <code>{}</code>. BigInt <strong>throws</strong>. Circular references <strong>throw</strong>.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-adjustments\"></i>Replacer, toJSON and reviver</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const user = { name: \"Ravi\", password: \"hunter2\", age: 30 };\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(user, [\"name\", \"age\"]));\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(user, (k, v) =&gt; (k === \"password\" ? undefined : v)));\n\nclass Money {\n  constructor(cents) { this.cents = cents; }\n  toJSON() { return `$${(this.cents / 100).toFixed(2)}`; }\n}\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify({ total: new Money(1999) }));\n\nconst text = '{\"when\":\"2024-01-15T10:00:00.000Z\",\"n\":1}';\nconst parsed = JSON.parse(text, (k, v) =&gt; (k === \"when\" ? new Date(v) : v));\nconsole.log(parsed.when instanceof Date, parsed.when.getUTCFullYear());</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>{\"name\":\"Ravi\",\"age\":30}\n{\"name\":\"Ravi\",\"age\":30}\n{\"total\":\"$19.99\"}\ntrue 2024</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-alert-circle\"></i>Errors</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>try {\n  JSON.parse(\"{name: 'x'}\");\n} catch (e) {\n  console.log(e.name);\n}\nconst a = { name: \"loop\" };\na.self = a;\ntry {\n  JSON.stringify(a);\n} catch (e) {\n  console.log(e.message.split(\"\\n\")[0]);\n}\ntry {\n  JSON.stringify({ n: 1n });\n} catch (e) {\n  console.log(e.message);\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>SyntaxError\nConverting circular structure to JSON\nDo not know how to serialize a BigInt</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--good\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Do</div><p>Always wrap <code>JSON.parse</code> of external input in <code>try/catch</code>, and validate the shape of what you get (a schema library like Zod) — valid JSON is not necessarily valid data.</p></div>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>Is JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(obj)) a good deep clone?</summary><div><p>Only for plain JSON-safe data. It drops <code>undefined</code>/functions/symbols, turns Dates into strings, Maps/Sets into <code>{}</code>, <code>NaN</code> into <code>null</code>, loses prototypes, and throws on BigInt and cycles. Use <code>structuredClone</code> instead.</p></div></details></section>"}